Diffusion-Based Inference. At inference, predictions are refined through T = 4 cumulative steps [86]. At each round of prediction, 25% of the predicted values are incorporated into the input expression profile. Previously revealed predictions remain fixed, resulting in a cumulative update across steps. In our implementation, gene positions are assigned random ranks r ∼ Uniform[0 , 1) G ′ . At step t , the model predicts the full profile from the current (partially updated) input; genes with r g ≤ α t (for α t ∈ { 0 . 25 , 0 . 5 , 0 . 75 , 1 . 0 } ) that were not already revealed are accepted (clamped to ≥ 0) and scattered back into the input for the next step. The mask M pert is updated correspondingly. This cumulative mode enables iterative coarse-to-fine refinement of the predictions (see Algorithm A.4 in the Appendix).
